---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Best OutDoor Wears"
  description="How Best OutDoor Wears handles data: what we collect, cookies and analytics, third-party links, and your rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose legal-page" style="max-width:74ch; padding-top:20px;">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mono" style="font-size:0.8rem;">Last updated: August 24, 2026</p>

      <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains what information Best OutDoor Wears ("we," "us") collects when you visit
        bestoutdoorwears.com, how it's used, and your choices. This is a small, independently run content site,
        not a data-driven platform — we collect as little as possible.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics:</strong> if analytics software is installed on this site, it may collect standard,
        non-identifying technical data (pages visited, approximate location by country/region, device type,
        referring site) to understand how the site is used. <strong>Purchases:</strong> if you buy TrailReady,
        payment and order information is collected and processed directly by our payment provider (Payhip or
        Gumroad), not by us — we don't see or store your payment card details.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site may use basic cookies for analytics purposes. You can disable cookies in your browser settings
        at any time; the site will still function normally without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party and affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site go to third-party retailers or brands, including affiliate links (see our
        <a href={url('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>). Those sites have their own privacy policies,
        which we don't control.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can request details of any data we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, by contacting us at the
        email on our <a href={url('/contact/')}>contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
